    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm doing a quick audit on a new fintech app we're building. Can you give me a checklist of the main WCAG 2.1 requirements I should look for regarding color contrast and screen reader compatibility?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For color contrast, ensure all text and essential UI components meet at least WCAG 2.1 AA standards, requiring a contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for regular text. When reviewing screen reader compatibility, verify that all informative images and non-text elements have accurate and descriptive alternative (alt) text. Additionally, check that interactive elements are properly labeled with ARIA roles so assistive technologies can correctly announce their function to users.",
