    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm mostly worried about the small stuff though—like when things look fine on a desktop but the accessibility breaks on a mobile view, or when there are weird little glitches in the UI that don't seem to have a clear cause. How should I document those kinds of edge cases or unexpected errors in my report?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Documenting these edge cases requires thorough context, so for mobile/responsive issues, note the exact viewport size or device type that causes the failure. For UI glitches, always record a step-by-step reproduction guide, including any specific user actions taken before the error appeared. Using screenshots or screen recordings alongside clear, descriptive bug titles will greatly help developers replicate and prioritize these unexpected issues.",
      "source": "target",
